@startuml
' Figure 13-1: three matching loci (models a / b / c) all discharging the paper's CLTS
' obligation on the SAME c(ℓ)-labelled firing. The SOURCE REWRITE (a rewrite of t at
' location ℓ) maps to opcorr: one firing corresponds to one 𝔅-transition labelled c(ℓ).
'   model a (paper's sugar): match decided IN Rho by nested single-name receives over the
'     per-location [[L]] spread -- non-atomic, can partially fire (RISK, amber).
'   model b (host-matched stepping-stone): match decided ON host via the Dovetail set
'     automaton + merge_substs, firing one flat (k+1)-ary sigma-receiver in ONE atomic COMM (SAFE, green).
'   model c (LANDED, in-Rho set automaton): match decided IN Rho by the compiled sa: automaton
'     network, keeping model b's atomic sigma-receiver and recovering O1 (SAFE, green).
' All three converge on the SAME c(ℓ) firing => same CLTS => invisible downstream (Q2, Q3).
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName monospaced
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #4A5568
skinparam ArrowFontColor #4A5568
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #4A5568
  FontColor #1A202C
  roundCorner 10
}

title Figure 13-1 — Three loci, one firing\nmodels a / b / c all land on the same <latex>c(\ell)</latex>-labelled firing <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> same CLTS

rectangle "SOURCE REWRITE\na rewrite of <latex>t</latex> at location <latex>\ell</latex>\n<latex>t \Rightarrow \mathit{rhs}(\sigma)</latex>" as SRC #DCEEF9
rectangle "THE PAPER'S CLTS OBLIGATION (opcorr)\none firing  <latex>\Leftrightarrow</latex>  one <latex>\mathfrak{B}</latex>-transition\nlabelled <latex>c(\ell) = \ulcorner\ell\urcorner</latex>" as OBL #E6DBF2

rectangle "model a — paper's sugar\nmatch decided IN Rho\nnested single-name receives + name-equality\nguards over the per-location <latex>[\![L]\!]</latex> spread\n(non-atomic; can partially fire — RISK)" as MA #FBE0B8
rectangle "model b — host-matched stepping-stone\nmatch decided ON host\nDovetail set automaton + merge_substs <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> <latex>\sigma</latex>\nflat <latex>(k{+}1)</latex>-ary <latex>\sigma</latex>-receiver on <latex>c(\ell)</latex>:\n<latex>\mathtt{for}(\sigma,\mathit{out} \Leftarrow c(\ell))\{\,\mathit{out}\,!\,([\![R]\!]\sigma)\,\}</latex>\n(single atomic COMM — SAFE)" as MB #C6E7D2
rectangle "model c — LANDED (in-Rho set automaton)\nmatch decided IN Rho\nby the sa: compiled automaton network;\nredex located + bound by interpreter COMMs\nsame flat <latex>\sigma</latex>-receiver; recovers O1\n(single atomic COMM — SAFE)" as MC #A7D8B6

rectangle "SAME <latex>c(\ell)</latex>-labelled firing, same resting state\n<latex>\Rightarrow</latex> same CLTS   <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> invisible downstream (Q2, Q3)" as FIRE #BFE3F2

SRC -down-> OBL : discharges
OBL -down-> MA
OBL -down-> MB
OBL -down-> MC
MA -down-> FIRE
MB -down-> FIRE
MC -down-> FIRE

note bottom of MA #FCEFD6
  the campaign red-team **refuted** model a:
  channel-incoherence, no linearity pass,
  wrong de-Bruijn indexing
end note
note right of FIRE #EAF2FB
  the paper certifies the equivalence (Q2, Q3):
  the optimal and the present scheme induce
  the same context-labelled transition system
end note
@enduml
